Grove PATCH-34: the mercy tx signed against the wrong pubkey hash on Particl

Found 2026-09-12 finishing ZANO's regtest matrix. Both ZANO swipe-refund cases
ended in BID_ERROR on every engine tried, 0.18.6+p32 and v0.18.7 alike, while the
same cases with BITCOIN as chain A passed. The swipe itself always succeeded --
the bid reached XMR_SWAP_FAILED_SWIPED_SENDING_MERCY and our side was paid -- and
then Particl refused the mercy transaction:

    RPC error {'code': -26, 'message': 'mandatory-script-verify-flag-failed
      (Signature must be zero for failed CHECK(MULTI)SIG operation)'}

The mercy tx is the courtesy payment that hands the counterparty back the
keyshare they need to recover. Failing it costs us nothing and costs THEM the
recovery, and leaves the bid in BID_ERROR rather than XMR_SWAP_FAILED_SWIPED.

THE BUG

BTCInterface.createMercyTx builds the scriptCode by slicing the prevout script:

    prevout_script[2:22]

which is the pubkey hash of a P2WPKH (0014<20 bytes>) and of nothing else.
BTCInterface.getScriptForPubkeyHash does return P2WPKH -- but PARTInterface
overrides it:

    BTC : CScript([OP_0, pkh])                                  -> 0014<hash>
    PART: CScript([OP_DUP, OP_HASH160, pkh, OP_EQUALVERIFY, ...]) -> 76a914<hash>88ac

On P2PKH the hash starts one byte later. Instrumenting a live Particl swipe
showed the slice taking the push opcode plus 19 of the 20 hash bytes:

    payout spk   76a914 9c31b6846171f9b770c305c0d6a83521c304ed82 88ac
    script_code  76a914 149c31b6846171f9b770c305c0d6a83521c304ed 88ac

Wrong sighash, invalid signature, NULLFAIL. A coin overrode the script shape and
a consumer of that script kept Bitcoin's byte layout -- the paired-site defect
this project keeps meeting.

THE FIX

Derive the scriptCode from the KEY rather than from the prevout script's bytes.
The scriptCode for a P2WPKH input (BIP143) and for a legacy P2PKH input are both
the P2PKH script of that pubkey hash, so this is correct for every coin and
deletes the layout assumption instead of special-casing Particl.

VERIFICATION

test_06_ads_part_coin_swipe_refund, which had failed on every prior run:

    Ran 1 test in 141.850s
    OK

with zero NULLFAIL rejections, against v0.18.7 with the fingerprint gate armed.

WHAT THIS DOES NOT APPLY TO, corrected after asserting the opposite

An earlier draft of this header said "applies to v0.18.7 and v0.18.6 -- the code
is identical in both". That is FALSE and was not checked before writing it.
`prevout_script[2:22]` does not exist in v0.18.6 at all:

    0.18.6 deployed (linux)   prevout_script[2:22] = 0 occurrences
    0.18.6 deployed (win)     prevout_script[2:22] = 0 occurrences
    v0.18.7 staged            prevout_script[2:22] = 1 occurrence

v0.18.6's createMercyTx has no key-signing branch: it ends in
`signTxWithWallet(tx.serialize())` unconditionally, and `swipePaysKey` does not
exist there. So on v0.18.6 the mercy tx is always wallet-signed, and it fails on
a Particl swipe because the payout went to a swap-derived key the wallet does not
hold -- same NULLFAIL symptom, different cause.

That makes upstream's v0.18.7 swipe/mercy rework the RIGHT fix for the v0.18.6
fault, carrying a one-byte bug of its own. This patch completes it rather than
working around it.

Consequence worth stating: this patch CANNOT repair the deployed v0.18.6 engine,
because the code it corrects is not there. A working mercy path on Particl
requires v0.18.7 + this patch.

Applies to: basicswap v0.18.7 only.

diff --git a/basicswap/interface/btc/btc.py b/basicswap/interface/btc/btc.py
--- a/basicswap/interface/btc/btc.py
+++ b/basicswap/interface/btc/btc.py
@@ -5135,11 +5135,35 @@
 
         # A key derived for this swap instead, which the wallet does not hold, so
         # nothing else can spend the output and it is signed here.
+        # PWNDA-PATCH-34: derive the scriptCode from the KEY, not by slicing the
+        # prevout script at a fixed offset.
+        #
+        # prevout_script[2:22] is the pubkey hash of a P2WPKH (0014<20>) and of
+        # nothing else. BTCInterface.getScriptForPubkeyHash returns P2WPKH, but
+        # PARTInterface OVERRIDES it to P2PKH (76a914<20>88ac), where the hash
+        # starts one byte later. Measured on a live Particl swipe:
+        #
+        #   payout spk   76a914 9c31b6846171f9b770c305c0d6a83521c304ed82 88ac
+        #   script_code  76a914 149c31b6846171f9b770c305c0d6a83521c304ed 88ac
+        #
+        # -- the push opcode plus 19 of the 20 hash bytes. Wrong sighash, invalid
+        # signature, and Particl refuses the mercy tx:
+        #
+        #   RPC error {'code': -26, 'message': 'mandatory-script-verify-flag-failed
+        #     (Signature must be zero for failed CHECK(MULTI)SIG operation)'}
+        #
+        # The swipe still pays, so no funds are lost -- but the counterparty never
+        # gets the keyshare the mercy tx exists to hand back, and the bid ends in
+        # BID_ERROR instead of XMR_SWAP_FAILED_SWIPED.
+        #
+        # The scriptCode for a P2WPKH input (BIP143) and for a legacy P2PKH input
+        # are both the P2PKH script of that pubkey hash, so deriving it from `key`
+        # is correct for every coin and removes the layout assumption entirely.
         script_code = CScript(
             [
                 OP_DUP,
                 OP_HASH160,
-                prevout_script[2:22],
+                self.pkh(self.getPubkey(key)),
                 OP_EQUALVERIFY,
                 OP_CHECKSIG,
             ]
